      {
        "id": "little-warthog-16",
        "type": "customfunction",
        "x": 2757,
        "y": 6185,
        "width": 160,
        "height": 88,
        "socketArray": [
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "data": "(brand) => {\n  return `<div class=\"font-sans bg-gray-50 p-4 border border-gray-300 rounded-md\">\n    <!-- Post Header -->\n    <div class=\"flex items-center mb-3\">\n      <div class=\"w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-orange-500 mr-2 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xs\">r/</div>\n      <div>\n        <h1 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-black\">r/programming</h1>\n        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Posted by u/devguru 5h ago</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- Post Content -->\n    <h2 class=\"text-lg font-medium mb-2 text-black\">I've been using ${brand} for a month now - here's my review</h2>\n    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-800 leading-relaxed mb-3\">\n      <p class=\"mb-2\">Hey everyone, I've been working with ${brand} for about a month now on a complex project, and I wanted to share my experience.</p>\n      \n      <p class=\"mb-2\">The good:</p>\n      <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mb-2 space-y-0.5\">\n        <li>The node-based system is incredibly intuitive</li>\n        <li>Being able to mix visual programming with custom code is a game changer</li>\n        <li>Performance is surprisingly good, even with complex graphs</li>\n      </ul>\n      \n      <p>Overall, I'm impressed. Has anyone else tried it for production work?</p>\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- Post Actions -->\n    <div class=\"flex items-center text-gray-500 text-xs mb-4 border-b border-gray-200 pb-3\">\n      <div class=\"flex items-center mr-4\">\n        <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-4 w-4 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M5 15l7-7 7 7\" />\n        </svg>\n        <span class=\"font-medium text-orange-500\">142</span>\n        <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-4 w-4 ml-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M19 9l-7 7-7-7\" />\n        </svg>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center mr-4\">\n        <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-4 w-4 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z\" />\n        </svg>\n        <span>67 comments</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n        <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-4 w-4 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n          <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M8.684 13.342C8.886 12.938 9 12.482 9 12c0-.482-.114-.938-.316-1.342m0 2.684a3 3 0 110-2.684m0 2.684l6.632 3.316m-6.632-6l6.632-3.316m0 0a3 3 0 105.367-2.684 3 3 0 00-5.367 2.684zm0 9.316a3 3 0 105.368 2.684 3 3 0 00-5.368-2.684z\" />\n        </svg>\n        <span>Share</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- Comment 1 -->\n    <div class=\"mb-3 pl-2 border-l-2 border-gray-200\">\n      <div class=\"flex\">\n        <div class=\"flex-grow\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline mb-1\">\n            <span class=\"font-medium text-xs mr-2\">TechBro42</span>\n            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">4h ago</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n            I've been using ${brand} for a couple of projects too. The custom function node is a lifesaver when you need to do something the standard nodes don't support.\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"flex items-center text-xs text-gray-500 mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mr-2\">\n              <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-3 w-3 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n                <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M5 15l7-7 7 7\" />\n              </svg>\n              <span>38</span>\n            </div>\n            <button class=\"mr-2 hover:text-gray-700\">Reply</button>\n            <button class=\"hover:text-gray-700\">Share</button>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Nested Reply -->\n          <div class=\"ml-4 pl-2 border-l-2 border-gray-200\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-baseline mb-1\">\n              <span class=\"font-medium text-xs mr-1 text-blue-600\">devguru</span>\n              <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-xs px-1 rounded mr-1\">OP</span>\n              <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">3h ago</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n              Yeah, I've connected it to a few REST APIs and it was surprisingly smooth. Much cleaner than my previous approach!\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"flex items-center text-xs text-gray-500\">\n              <div class=\"flex items-center mr-2\">\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-3 w-3 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n                  <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M5 15l7-7 7 7\" />\n                </svg>\n                <span>12</span>\n              </div>\n              <button class=\"mr-2 hover:text-gray-700\">Reply</button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- Comment 2 -->\n    <div class=\"mb-3 pl-2 border-l-2 border-gray-200\">\n      <div class=\"flex\">\n        <div class=\"flex-grow\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-baseline mb-1\">\n            <span class=\"font-medium text-xs mr-2\">SkepticalCoder</span>\n            <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">3h ago</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n            How does it handle version control? That's always been my biggest issue with visual programming tools.\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"flex items-center text-xs text-gray-500\">\n            <div class=\"flex items-center mr-2\">\n              <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"h-3 w-3 mr-1\" fill=\"none\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke=\"currentColor\">\n                <path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M5 15l7-7 7 7\" />\n              </svg>\n              <span>24</span>\n            </div>\n            <button class=\"mr-2 hover:text-gray-700\">Reply</button>\n            <button class=\"hover:text-gray-700\">Share</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <!-- More Comments Link -->\n    <button class=\"w-full py-2 text-center text-sm text-blue-500 hover:bg-gray-100 rounded-md\">\n      View more comments\n    </button>\n  </div>`;\n}",
