      {
        "id": "helpless-duck-76",
        "type": "customfunction",
        "x": 2751,
        "y": 2231,
        "width": 160,
        "height": 112,
        "socketArray": [
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "data": "(brand, noun) => {\n\treturn `## Brand Name Evaluation\n\nYou are an expert brand strategist with experience in naming tech products and services. I need your professional analysis on a proposed brand name and its associated branded noun.\n\n**Brand Name:** ${brand}\n**Branded Noun:** ${noun}\n*(Example: Twitter is the brand name, Tweet is the branded noun)*\n\nPlease provide a comprehensive evaluation covering:\n\n### Part 1: Brand Name Analysis\n- **Memorability:** How easily remembered is the brand name?\n- **Distinctiveness:** How it stands out from competitors\n- **Pronunciation:** Clarity and ease of saying it aloud\n- **Domain availability:** Likelihood of securing related domains\n- **Semantic meaning:** What it naturally evokes or suggests\n- **International considerations:** Any potential issues in other languages/cultures\n- **Legal concerns:** Potential trademark issues or similarities to existing brands\n\n### Part 2: Branded Noun Analysis\n- **Natural usage:** How naturally it can be used in sentences (\"I just sent a Tweet\")\n- **Verb potential:** Can it function as a verb? (\"I Tweeted about it\")\n- **Clarity:** How clearly it communicates what the user is creating/sharing\n- **Consistency:** How well it aligns with the brand name\n- **Uniqueness:** How distinct it is from common terms\n\n### Part 3: Overall Brand Language\n- **Pros:** Top 3 strengths of this brand name + branded noun combination\n- **Cons:** Top 3 weaknesses or concerns with this combination\n- **Overall rating:** On a scale of 1-10, how effective is this naming strategy?\n\n### Part 4: Alternatives\nSuggest 2-3 alternative combinations of brand name and branded noun that might be more effective, with a brief explanation of why each might work better.\n\nPlease format your response with clear headings and bullet points for easy readability.\n`;\n}",
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Main Thread",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"BooleanType\"}",
            "data": false,
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "brand",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "noun",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "OutData",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "visible": false
          }
        ],
        "updateBehaviour": {
          "load": true,
          "update": true,
          "interval": false
        },
        "version": 3
      },
